  "result": "Here's what I found: the site builds the timetable from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. That file has no way to mark a sailing as cancelled, and the site has no warning code yet. So the hard part isn't showing the warning. It's how the site finds out a sailing is cancelled at all. Also, cancellations probably often happen on the day itself, after the nightly export has already gone out.\n\nWhat happens today when a sailing gets cancelled: who decides it, how soon do they know, and how does word reach passengers right now? Your answer tells me where the site should get cancellations from and how quickly a warning has to appear.\n\nOr if you'd rather I just dive in, say so.",
